Apple Inc.'s stock (AAPL) rose 0.3% in afternoon trade, putting it on track for the sixth-straight gain. The 11.8% the stock has climbed during that streak, which began after it closed at a four-month low on Feb. 8, would be the biggest six-session percentage gain since it climbed 12.7% in the six sessions ending May 1, 2014. That six-day rally was kicked off by better-than-expected fiscal second-quarter results (https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/320193/000119312514154871/d715148dex991.htm) and after the company boosted its capital return program to $130 billion (https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/320193/000119312514154883/d715379dex991.htm). The stock's current bounce coincides with the bounce in the broader stock market (http://www.marketwatch.com/story/dow-ready-to-hold-above-25000-as-us-stocks-line-up-best-week-more-than-a-year-2018-02-16). The Dow has rallied 1,426 points, or 6.0%, amid a six-session win streak.
-Tomi Kilgore;
 1524ET
